      > includes a folding canister stove and a pot in one package.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="takeaways">
    <strong>Key takeaways</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Canister stoves are the simplest and most common choice for an <a
          href="/guides/overnight-hike-packing-list/">overnight hike</a
        >: light, fast-boiling, easy to control.
      </li>
      <li>
        Alcohol and solid fuel stoves are lighter again but slower to boil and
        harder to simmer with.
      </li>
      <li>
        Integrated systems boil water fastest per gram of fuel but cost more and
        are less flexible for actual cooking. Think of them as an optional
        upgrade.
      </li>
      <li>
        Screw-top butane-propane canisters are the easiest fuel to buy in
        Australia; metho and solid fuel tablets are also widely stocked.
      </li>
